  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CLARE - MET Office - INHFL - International Natural Hazard Forward Look</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The International Natural Hazard Forward Look (&#x2018;INHFL&#x2019;) system provides a global, multi-hazard forward-looking system that aims to allow UK government departments and their partners to be more anticipatory, resulting in earlier decision making and reducing the impacts of future natural hazard related disasters. It includes consideration of both rapid and slow-onset natural hazards worldwide.
The Met Office will provide the Government Office for Science (GO-Science) with the INHFL in collaboration with Public Health England (PHE), DEFRA&#x2019;s Animal and Plant Health Agency (APHA) the British Geological Survey (BGS) and the GO- Science (the &#x2018;Contributors&#x2019;).</narrative>
  </description>
